    "title": "Jade Cargill Says She Gets Paid By The Match, Jey Uso Tells Fans To 'Chill' After Backlash - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Sap Sinha ,\n1 hours ago\nJade Cargill has promised a more ruthless approach when she challenges Rhea Ripley at WWE Clash In Italy.\nDuring a recent appearance on ESPN’s First Take, Cargill said she made a big mistake at WrestleMania 42 by soaking in the crowd and not finishing Ripley when she had her beaten.\nCargill claims she will now go straight for the kill shot, strike when the iron is hot, and not play with her food. The former AEW TBS Champion wants to make the rematch quick, as she gets paid by the match, not by the second.\nJade Cargill also explained why she often refuses to sign autographs in public.\nREAD MORE: Bully Ray Blasts Oba Femi, John Cena Explains Shift From WWE To Hollywood, Rhea Ripley/Jacob Fatu\nREAD MORE: Liv Morgan’s Defenseless Title Reign Adressed By Roxanne Perez\nDuring a recent appearance on the “Unsportsmanlike” podcast, Cargill revealed that whi;e William Regal and her husband urged her to sign more, she wants to protect kayfabe and keep fans hating her as a heel.\nCargill explained she is naturally kind, which can make fans want to cheer her, so she keeps her distance unless children are involved. She also warned adults not to use kids to get extra items signed, and that people thinking she has an attitude actually helps her get louder boos at shows.\nJey Uso has responded to fan backlash after missing the May 25 episode of WWE RAW.\nThe former WWE World Heavyweight Champion reminded fans on Instagram that he only took one Monday off and asked them to “chill.”\nJey recently faced criticism for calling himself the best “world entertainment wrestler” and said he does not understand why his confidence upsets people.\nJey Uso responds to fan backlash on Instagram.",
    "summary": "Jade Cargill has promised a more ruthless approach when she challenges Rhea Ripley at WWE Clash In Italy. During a recent appearance on ESPN’s First Take, Cargill said she made a big mistake at WrestleMania 42 by soaking in the crowd and not finishing Ripley when she had her beaten. Cargill claims she will now go straight for the kill shot, strike when the iron is hot, and not play with her food.",
